vectors.json: ground truth for muster's model of the quest record program (lez/quest.nim,
exo-267.7, docs/design/lez-quest-program.md).

It was generated by the program's own crate, quest_core, the types its program
(run_program(plan, apply) on LEZ v0.3.0) reads and writes: the binary `vectors` in the
quest_e2e package of programs/lez-quest (e2e/src/bin/vectors.rs).

Regenerate it (build needs as in infra/lez/localnet.sh's header: a C++ compiler, libclang; a
binary built with nixpkgs#gcc also needs nix's libstdc++ to run):

  cd programs/lez-quest
  RISC0_SKIP_BUILD=1 cargo build --release -p quest_e2e --bin vectors
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<nixpkgs#gcc.cc^lib>/lib target/release/vectors > ../../module/tests/vectors/lez-quest-v010/vectors.json

Generated 2026-11-09.

What it pins, for a program account 0x11…, issuer 0x01…, taker 0x02…, confirmer 0x03…, quest id
0x09…, terms hash 0x05…, bounty 250:
- the record seed, SHA-256("/lez-quest/v0.1/Record/" padded to 32 ‖ issuer ‖ quest id), and its
  PDA, SHA-256("/LEE/v0.2/AccountId/PDA/" padded ‖ program account ‖ seed);
- QuestRecord borsh in each status: Open (no taker named, and one named), Accepted, Confirmed,
  Closed (each carrying the taker), Cancelled;
- every Instruction's borsh: Open (open and named), Accept, Confirm, Close, Cancel.
